  "text": "An en dash with a space on each side, ` \u2013 `, separates the fields of every heading, label, subject, and metadata line that the runtime, the terminal display, the browser viewer, the presentation decks, the landing page, and the documentation print; the middle dot `\u00b7` is not a field separator anywhere. A tool subject reads `cargo test -p parser \u2013 exit 0 in 1.50s`; a session line reads `session 2: postgres \u2013 alive`; the telemetry preview joins its heading and its totals with ` \u2013 `; the terminal display prints `lead \u2013 You`, `reviewer \u2013 Completed`, and `Final \u2013 Completed`; and the viewer's rendering, fixtures, and tests use the same character. The terminal display in crates/view names the separator in one constant, `FIELD`, and every heading it prints reads that constant.\n\nThe middle dot has three uses that are not separators: the first and last frame of the brand pulse in docs/brand/README.md, the multiplication in `90\u00b0 + k\u00b760\u00b0` in the same document, and the middle dot the presentation decks set as a list marker. The vendored converter under view/vendor, the recorded episode logs under crates/telemetry/tests/fixtures, and the telemetry golden derived from them keep their bytes.\n\nEach part of the tree the change reaches is judged by the tests that cover it. checks/run.sh runs the check the whole change is judged on: cargo test --workspace, cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings, and scripts/loc.sh.\n\nThe documents under docs/ describe the behavior. Each sentence below belongs in the document named before it, in the same words:\n- docs/tools.md: cargo test -p parser \u2013 exit 0 in 1.50s, the command and how it ended\n- docs/tools.md: session 2: postgres \u2013 alive, 41 lines for a poll, session 2: exit 0 after 84s for a stop or for a poll after the end\n\nFollow AGENTS.md. Run the checks it names. When you finish, or when you cannot, report your outcome.",
